I'd ditch the quarterstaff even sooner and just use a dagger for melee
too.  As a Wizard you're supposed to avoid melee anyway, and the staff
ain't that good a weapon in the first place.  Ditching it will let you
carry more armor (or more wands, or more daggers, or even a pile of
darts if you're short on daggers), and using a dagger for melee too
lets you advance them faster.

There's something to be said for naming Sting as soon as you get a
(non-cursed) elven dagger and using it as your main melee weapon.  Of
course there's also something to be said against it (lower chance of
getting other artifacts later), but it _is_ a nice early-game weapon
if you want to specialize in daggers, and the warning and bonus
against orcs can be a lifesaver when they first start appearing.


